Fortran sources translated by radcor, unchanged from the 2005 distribution (README.slifer).

whitney/radcor.f          L. Whitney's SLAC code (Saclay version), based on G. Miller, SLAC-R-129.
                          Kept for reference only: it does not compile with current gfortran
                          (a DO variable is redefined, W:433). ele-input.old is its example input.
unpolarized/nradcor.f     K. Slifer's unpolarized version for JLab E94-010 ("U" in the manual).
                          correct.f: Slifer's small test program for the acceptance tables.
polarized/nradcor.f       K. Slifer's polarized version ("P" in the manual).

Slifer's description of his changes: ../doc/slifer_newcodes.pdf

Build:   make                    (gfortran; flags in the Makefile)
Run:     programs read and write fixed file names in the current directory:
           U: ele-input, input/*_qfs_finite_acceptance.out -> output/E94010_xs_unfolded.dat
           P: input/radcor_input.dat, input/ds.inp         -> output/ds.rc3
         e.g.  cd ../data/e94010/unpol && mkdir -p output && ../../../fortran/unpolarized/nradcor
Test:    ../tests/run_fortran_parity.sh builds both programs, runs them on data/e94010 and
         compares with data/e94010/*/expected and with the C++.
